# WN22-SO-000370: Windows Server 2022 default permissions of global system objects must be strengthened.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: low
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-so-000370-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `medium`

    title `Windows Server 2022 default permissions of global system objects must be strengthened.`
    description `Windows systems maintain a global list of shared system resources such as DOS device names, mutexes, and semaphores. Each type of object is created with a default Discretionary Access Control List (DACL) that specifies who can access the objects with what permissions. When this policy is enabled, the default DACL is stronger, allowing nonadministrative users to read shared objects but not to modify shared objects they did not create.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,registry,low,ksi-cmt-lmc,ksi-cmt-rmv,ksi-mla-evc,ksi-svc-acm`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-CMT-LMC,KSI:KSI-CMT-RMV,KSI:KSI-MLA-EVC,KSI:KSI-SVC-ACM,NIST-800-53:CM-6`
    control_objective `KSI-CMT-LMC,KSI-CMT-RMV,KSI-MLA-EVC,KSI-SVC-ACM`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `90`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> Security Options >> System objects: Strengthen default permissions of internal system objects (e.g., Symbolic Links) to "Enabled".`

    component_id `comp-windows-registry`

    impl_KSI_CMT_LMC `Windows Server implements KSI-CMT-LMC by setting registry value 'ProtectionMode' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session Manager' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_CMT_RMV `Windows Server implements KSI-CMT-RMV by setting registry value 'ProtectionMode' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session Manager' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_MLA_EVC `Windows Server implements KSI-MLA-EVC by setting registry value 'ProtectionMode' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session Manager' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_SVC_ACM `Windows Server implements KSI-SVC-ACM by setting registry value 'ProtectionMode' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session Manager' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_CM_6 `Windows Server implements CM-6 by setting registry value 'ProtectionMode' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session Manager' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        hive `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE`
        key `SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session Manager`
        name `ProtectionMode`
        behavior executor powershell
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int = 1
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN registry
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
